A||||3||BigBoyToys||New to forum - intermittent starting||||1
Z||000000||BigBoyToys||10-07-1999||08:47 PM||||I have been following this form for the past few months and think you all have a really great thing going here for all Fiero enthusiast. So I desided to register and kick in when I can. This summer I found the Fiero I was looking for a 86.5 GT fastback originally from California now in the NE for the past two years. When I first looked at it the owner was asking $2500 but did not have the title in his posession and said it was still tiltled in Calif. so I offered him $1500 and said to call me when he got the title I would get it in the shop and if it checked out I may go $2000. When he finally called me he indicated that the car was having some problems in that when he took it to work (approx 8 mile) after work it would not start again until 2 days later. To cut to the chase I got the car for $1700. He had replaced the ignition coil and module but not<BR>the pickup coil. The car was also running very rough, backfiring during deceloration and lacking in power. I started a tune-up as I do with all my toys when I get them, in this case I replaced Plugs (splitfire), cap,rotor,wires,air filter,oil and air filter. Took it for a ride, got gas (shut it off and it started) took it home went out an hour later and would not start. Turns over great but no start. Next day went out and it started rite up. I checked the engine code and found it was calling out the TPS so I replaced it and the IAC (for idling problem)<BR>and it now runs great, slight backfire and all new power but still intermitent starting.<BR>All I have read in this forum and other sources indicate that the pickup coil is a hard fail has anyone seen one go intermitent?<BR>Also bought a 84se for parts. Are steering rack & hyd clutch slave interchangable? Any insight would be much appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-07-1999||10:03 PM||||pull the tach filter off. they hate heat. they die. they short out the coil when they do.<P>If it still screws up replace the pickup. Yes the pickup could be intermitant.<P>pretty near everything in Fiero is interchangeable between years. There are only a few minor exceptions for V6. Only 88 suspension parts won't interchange with other years.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||10-08-1999||08:56 AM||||I believe I read a post a few days ago from the man himself (Ed Parks) about a faulty pickup coil.  He said the coil would read normal on a meter.  But after the car had wamed up, it would not restart.  Turned out the pickup coil had a hairline crack that, while fine, when cool and warming up, would expand, causing no more spark after the car had sufficiently warmed up, and was shut off.  This is possibile, I would replace it anyway, but I don't think it is the most likely cause at this point. Vapor lock? Leaky injector? etc... I have heard of all of these producing the same problem, but, probably not the culprit.  I would go with the tach filter on this one first also.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 10-08-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||10-08-1999||09:15 AM||||Also you should probably do a search for splitfire plugs here on the forum.  Several people have tried these and thier Fieros did not like them at all.<P>You might not have a problem, but it cant hurt to stay informed about things that others have tried and didnt like....<P>||||reg||1
